\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {39}{\ignorespaces This figure shows the drag reduction against iteration for the four pass-3 replicates on their own seeds. The markers show where each run doubled its seeds instead of stopping. Pass 3 used N\_REF = 250k, N\_AVG = 4, N\_AVG\_MAX = 32, N\_FOURIER = 10, GRAD\_INIT\_FRAC = 0.05, N\_ITER = 100 and SEED0 = 0, 100, 200 and 300.\relax }}{19}{figure.caption.40}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {40}{\ignorespaces This figure shows the drag reduction of every optimised shape on 16 unseen seeds, grouped by setting. Each dot is one run, and the bar marks the mean. Pass 3 used N\_REF = 250k, N\_AVG = 4, N\_AVG\_MAX = 32, N\_FOURIER = 10, GRAD\_INIT\_FRAC = 0.05, N\_ITER = 100 and SEED0 = 0, 100, 200 and 300.\relax }}{19}{figure.caption.41}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {41}{\ignorespaces This figure shows how the drag changes when the optimised shapes are stepped into the modes they did not use. The drag was re-measured on unseen seeds, and the error bars are $\pm 1$ standard error. Pass 3 used N\_REF = 250k, N\_AVG = 4, N\_AVG\_MAX = 32, N\_FOURIER = 10, GRAD\_INIT\_FRAC = 0.05, N\_ITER = 100 and SEED0 = 0, 100, 200 and 300.\relax }}{20}{figure.caption.42}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {42}{\ignorespaces This figure shows the best 5-mode and 10-mode shapes from pass 2 and the final 10-mode shape from pass 3, with their drag reductions on unseen seeds. All shapes have the same perimeter, and the gas flows from left to right. Pass 3 used N\_REF = 250k, N\_AVG = 4, N\_AVG\_MAX = 32, N\_FOURIER = 10, GRAD\_INIT\_FRAC = 0.05, N\_ITER = 100 and SEED0 = 0, 100, 200 and 300.\relax }}{20}{figure.caption.43}\protected@file@percent }
